# Automatic releases

Do **not** ask the user to bump `package.json` or run a manual release. Merging to the default branch tags (and optionally releases) automatically.

Prefer independent PRs against the default branch. Stacked PRs are allowed — after the base merges, Actions retargets children and auto-merges them.

When opening a PR, set **exactly one** label:

| Label | Use when | Bump |
|-------|----------|------|
| `release:major` | Breaking / incompatible behavior | `X.0.0` |
| `release:minor` | New user-facing capability | `x.Y.0` |
| `release:patch` | Fix, chore, docs, CI, refactor | `x.y.Z` |
| `release:skip` | No tag/release | — |

Default if unsure: **`release:patch`**.

```bash
gh pr create ... --label "release:minor"
```

Do not commit version bumps unless the user explicitly asks.
